{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/216255-demon-redescention-or-dtf-dtd-dtr","id":216255,"title":"Demon: Redescention, or DtF + DtD + DtR","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-01T16:16:24-07:00","id":216255,"title":"Demon: Redescention, or DtF + DtD + DtR","content":"<span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Or, welding together </span></span><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Demon: the Redemption</span></span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">,</span></span><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Demon: the Fallen</span></span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">and </span></span><i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Demon: the Descent</span></span></i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">. Angels who wrote the universe, a Demiurge with it's boot to the throat of the world, angels enforcing the divine workings of the demiurge, demons escaping the pit to possess humans, filled with Torment. Cool things. The general thrust of the setting will be this;</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Angels exist in the setting, and are at a cold war with the Fallen. Think the USSR and the US, the Pit is the home of the demons, and the Heavens for the Angels, the mortal world is where divine workings happens, where demons make pacts for souls.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Demons come from either the great Fall when the Universe broke (the Death of Father Wolf, the fall of Atlantis, ect) or from Angels who lose their way, and Fall themselves. Newly Fallen are pulled into the Pit and develop Torment like their brethren. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Cover is switched for Torment, which makes it easier for Angel's to sense demons, and deforms and harms the host of Demons, at 10 Torment a host will die (working idea. Replaces the idea of Covers going away at 0)</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Power-wise, I suggest using the Dominions of Demon: the Redemption. They represent powers corrupted from their Angelic Influences, giving them dominion over natural forces of the world, which the Houses helped write. (Cross over-wise, in my setting, the Angels are the one's who wrote the symbols that compose the Supernal Realms, and the Fallen were shoved into the Lower Depths where they mutated, and got corrupted; their True Names twisting to the Torments of the Pitt [Or perhaps the Inferno?])<br /> <br /> I love the concept of Occult <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Matrices, and wish to keep the basic idea, but stripping away the techgnostic facade, leaving only the Gnostic (hopefully). I'd call them 'Divine Workings' and have them, basically, like Imperial Rites. They require people, conditions, linchpins, to run. Probably replace Infrastructure and gears with occult places, ritual trappings, cults gathering Aether, and other such things.</span><br /> Edit: The Dominions written so far can be found here: </span><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mA35coEuBRSJFHY-C5_2rZqaIkurEsC0jwZAs7VpYo8/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...ZAs7VpYo8/edit</a><br /> Main Document: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hwL5JQSynlW2k0ygXyQ5Of_iGztEpTGPmN9L2cAdFsk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...9L2cAdFsk/edit</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\">Anyways, here are the Character Creation rules I have, so far;</span><br /> <b>Character Creation</b><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">5/4/3 to Attributes</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">11/7/4 to Skills</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">4 </span></span><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, times, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Specialties</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Choose a House</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Choose a Creed</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Pick two Dominions, one from your House, and the other from what you wish.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, times, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Create an Apocalyptic Form, 3 Transfigurations, 2 Projections, 1 Conveyance, and 1 Countenance. Then pick the High Torment traits for your form, 2 Transfigurations (or 2 Projections), 1 Projection (or 1 Transfiguration), 1 Conveyance, and 1 Countenance.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Select 10 Merit dots.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Create a (Demonic) Urge, and (Angelic) Purpose</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Create 3 Aspirations \u2013 1 long-term, 2 short-term</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Answer questions (Any help with the five questions for the Fallen?)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, times, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Calculate Advantages: Reminiscence is 1, Torment is 3, starting Aether is 10 \u2013 Torment, Speed is Strength + Dexterity + 5, Size is 5, Health is Stamina + Size, Willpower is Resolve + Composure, Defense is (lower of Wits and Dexterity) + Athletics, Initiative is Dexterity + Composure.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, times, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Innate Abilities of the Fallen</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Liar's Tongue: As per the Unchained</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Immunity to Possession: Because the Fallen are already humans possessed by the Tormented essence of a Fallen angel.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Invocation: System Pending</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Damage Resistance: In Apocalyptic Form, all Fallen have 1/1 Armor.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Apocalyptic Form: Demonic form, per Descent. Spend 1 Aether to shift into Apocalyptic Form, shifting back to Human is free; can spend any time you want in Apocalyptic form. May have an increase of Torment in Apocalyptic Form, not sure yet.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Aetheric Healing: Reflexive Action, 1 Faith per damage, Lethal before Bashing.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Language Knowledge: As per the Unchained.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Reminiscence</b> is the Power Stat of the Fallen, measuring how much they remember of their Angelic glory, and Demonic might. Raising your Reminiscence will be a sin against Torment (I'm not sure what level it will be). The Integrity stat for the Fallen is <b>Torment</b>. It measures how twisted the Fallen is by their time in the Lower Depths, and by their own hate. Torment is a reverse stat, 1 Torment is saintly, where Torment 10 is a complete monster. I will probably keep the concept of Temporary Torment points. Unlike a normal Morality stat, failing a Torment roll gives you a certain number of Temporary Torment points too your total; when you reach 10 temporary Torment points, your permanent Torment score goes up by 1. When you do deeds to drop your Torment, you subtract the points from temp. Torment points, until you get to 0, then you take a dot and subtract any remaining from the 9 left. (E.G, you get -2 Torment points and have only 1 temp. Torment, and 4 perm. Torment. You would make your perm score to 3, and gain 8 temp. Torment.)<br /> <br /> Fallen spend Aether which will be fluffed as the original stuff of Creation. A more refined Pyros, the stuff above Mana, a less base Essence. Moving it from the waste heat of the God-Machine, to the divine essence. Angels get theirs from Above, while Demons must harvest scraps of it from humans (or other ensouled beings) with acts of Revelation. Which do give the mortal a Breaking Point... that's up for the demons to debate the morality of it. Cults are another source of Aether for the Fallen. Many of the demonic Cultists are in a pact with them, and are at Reminiscence 0 with a Minor template.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's about the extent of the system I have so far, if you have any critiques, suggestions, or something you want to see, please do so.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 08-12-2014, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T14:12:33-07:00","id":216912,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">On Angels, and the Demiurge</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Angels, servants of the high heavens, implacable enemies of the Fallen, and former comrades. You come from the same source, but are part of two different cultures, and existences now. In </span><i>Demon: the Descent</i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">, a lot of the horror of facing the God-Machine's angels was the fact they could take you back, and remake you. Losing your free-will, or just be used for spare parts. The Fallen are different, and the Elohim are different than the angels of the God-Machine. Still Gnostic, and still deadly, implacable foes. What makes them scary? My wife suggests that the Elohim can still recycle a demon who's host is destroyed, and who goes into Twilight form. They can cart off the shell of the Fallen back to Heaven and remake you into an angel. Personally, I think this makes the Integrator/Reconciler Creed nonsensical. If one of the Creeds wishes to be redeemed, isn't the easiest way to throw one's self into the arms of the Hunter seraph and let it recycle your celestial essence into a pure, non-Tormented form? It seems to easy for me. It's an interesting idea. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">I've established that the Demiurge still makes new angels for Missions, but when the celestial Truename is brought into existence, and it's symbol and form spun it's eternal. It lasts for a long time, perhaps an eternity. The reason that the Fallen are, well, Fallen is because angels do not mutilate, and cannot truly kill their own. It's why the Fallen fear the Pit, nothing can end the torture, and the it's twisting effect. Or perhaps, the Celestial arn't that tough, they can be killed? Perhaps it's part of the Fallen's curse that they are always consumed by the Inferno, and the angelic host can die, or that the crafty Demiurge can bring one of the Fallen before him and get a new servant. One of the ideas I had is that Reconcilers KNOW that God is gone, and an impostor sits upon the Throne of Heaven. The Reconciler's new goal would be working with, and convincing Angels of this, and perhaps looking for a way the Demiurge. They'd need to stay pure themselves, because they view themselves as Angels who were screwed over for knowing the truth. This is thematic, but changes the direction of Reconciler's quite a bit. I'm leaning towards the last one, but am not sure about the subject of the Elohim being able to turn demons into angels, I'm not sure if it's thematic to this hack.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Moving on. I mentioned the Fallen and Angels having a truename. Much like Fallen (and Redemption) both the Fallen and Elohim possess Celestial names, and Truenames. The Celestial name is what you use to cast an Invocation (or listen on to it) when a Celestial name is spoken, the being that possess that Celestial name can listen in on, or establish a two way connection. It gives a way for Angels and demons to talk. Or the Fallen to talk to their fellows. It's much like getting the cellphone number of the specific being. (except with added perks). When an Angel or Demon uses their senses to investigate Aetheric Resonance, they can pull a portion of the user's Truename, or their Celestial name from the sense of the Resonance. Truenames allow greater control over your victim, making abilities easier to use against them, it gives you a sense of their Angelic Purpose, and Demonic Urge. That kind of stuff.<br /> <br /> Also, I've gotten permission to translate Demon: the Redemption, and at the very least, I will do so for the Dominions, and post them in a GoogleDoc for all to see, if you're interested.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 08-02-2014, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T14:26:28-07:00","id":218508,"title":"","content":"<b>Embeds &amp; Dominions (and the Cipher)</b><br /> I've been thinking recently. Dominions are nice, BIG effects that the Fallen can use. It touches upon their nature as creators of the universe, Embeds (Which I need a new name for? Any suggestions) touch on the aspect of 'secrets paths of the universe' which make as much sense for the Fallen as it does the Unchained. It also gives cheap, subtle, powers for the Fallen to get, and it also opens up using the Cipher for the Fallen. Mr. Paurdo's hack for DtD names his (more demonic) demons as their 'Malpraxis' which is a good, thematic name, but I'm bouncing two ideas to what the Cipher (Malpraxis?) for the Fallen is. One is that it's something the Creator encoded into them, that they only realize when they Fall. Perhaps hinting at the Fallen were supposed to always Fall. Or, I was thinking that the Cipher can go down two paths, one when the Demon starts to redeem himself, and become more Angelic, or one where they embrace their new nature (Beneficence and Malpraxis? Maybe Stupid Loserman's suggestion of Mysteries would work better). In any case, this new Cipher would be tied to an integral Dominion and Embeds that they buy, otherwise, it's built much like an Unchained's Cipher just flavored by the chosen Dominion(s?). <br /> <br /> Speaking of Dominions, not everyone is familiar with Redemption. The Dominions are, basically, corrupted Angelic Influences. They are aspects of reality that the Fallen can control with their Aether. Things like the Dominion of Flames allows the Fallen to manipulate, strengthen, create, and basically have Dominion of fire. One's like the Dominion of Radiance is about controlling people with a supernatural Radiance (think Presence from Vampire), Dominion of Ghosts allows one to, you guessed it, interact with and control the Dead.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Embeds, Cover, and Torment</b></span></span><br /> Now, Embeds sometimes require a Demon to make a compromise check. Now, the Fallen don't HAVE Cover, they have Torment. Now, I haven't homed in on what Torment entails. My initial thought is that any time a Fallen uses a Dominion's Evocation they roll for Torment (Resolve + Composure + Reminiscence) with a modifier based on how high or low their Permanent Torment is (Below 3 = +2, and above 6 = -2) with extra minuses if the Fallen tries spending more than their natural limit of Aether on an Evocation (so if a low Reminiscence Fallen can only spend 1 Aether per turn, but wants to use a 3 Aether Evocation when they finally cast it, it will be at a -2 to the Torment roll) this allows for most powers to have a slim chance of Evoking Torment, but keeps it a risk. Purposely Evoking Torment gives you 1 temp. Torment automatically. Tormened Evocation are always more destructive, and harming. In some situations it should be tempting to Evoke Torment on your Evocation, but that comes with a price. For instance, a Evocation of the Dominion of Flames may cause the fire to grow larger, and hotter while it turns an unnatural color, and spreads more than the Fallen intended. This may be helpful in hurting additional antagonists, but it may also harm allies. <br /> The intent is to have Torment replace the compromise checks of Exploits. With that said, Torment can be sensed by Aetheric Senses, and Angels are attuned to the dark energies, and can pick up Torment at a range depending on the amount of Aether that was spent on the Tormented Evocation. <br /> <br /> I've noticed that not a lot of replies have been here. I will continue to update this, but I am up for any critique or suggestions. To those watching, thanks. My wife and I are working on translating <i>Demon: the Redemption</i>'s Dominions to English and as soon as that is done, I will post them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 08-04-2014, 09:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T15:35:30-07:00","id":220496,"title":"","content":"Some more systems to peruse. I'll start putting up translated Doinions soon. Before that I'll include a list of all the Dominions, but what they do should be pretty evident from their name.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Seven Houses </b>(The Sebettu)<br /> <br /> <b>Halaku,</b> the Slayers<br /> <b>Formula</b>: Mundane<br /> <b>Dominion</b>: Dominion of Death, Dominion of Darkness, Dominion of Ghosts, Dominion of Cold<br /> <br /> <b>Niberu, </b>the Fiends<br /> <b>Formula</b>: Instrumental<br /> <b>Dominions:</b> Dominion of Probability, Dominion of Prophecy, Dominion of Time, Dominion of Illusions<br /> <br /> <b>Lammasu</b>, the Seducers<br /> <b>Formula:</b> Vocal<br /> <b>Dominions</b>: Dominion of Dreams, Dominion of Sin, Dominion of the Body, Dominion of the Voice<br /> <br /> <b>Namaru</b>, the Devils<br /> <b>Formula</b>: Pick any one at character creation<br /> <b>Dominions</b>: Dominion of the Celestial, Dominion of Flames, Dominion of Radiance, Dominion of Light<br /> <br /> <b>Rabisu</b>, the Devourers<br /> <b>Formula</b>: Cocophany<br /> <b>Dominions</b>: Dominion of Beasts, Dominion of Metamorphosis, Dominion of Wilds, Dominion of Weather<br /> <br /> <b>Asharu</b>, the Scourge<br /> <b>Formula</b>: Instrumental<br /> <b>Dominions</b>: Dominion of Life, Dominion of Diseases, Dominion of the Winds, Dominion of Firmaments<br /> <br /> <b>Belbresu</b>, the Malefactors<br /> <b>Formula:</b> Mundane<br /> <b>Dominions:</b> Dominion of Earth, Dominion of the Forge, Dominion of Materials, Dominion of Objects<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Special Systems</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Faith as a Weapon</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The mortal's higher self is a fearsome thing to behold when it is levied against the demon. A mortal who starts an Abjuration (page 231 of the <i>God-Machine Chronicles</i>), and beats the Demon's Presence + Resolve with their Resolve + Composure rolls inflicts the Abjured Condition upon the Demon.</span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Abjured</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">A faithful mortal has Abjured you with his higher self. You find yourself unable to aproach or harm the mortal. Any attempts to approach the mortal fail, and you suffer a -5 to all actions within sight of the mortal. Attempting to attack the mortal causes you to take your Torment points in Bashing damage, and you do not successfully attack.</span><br /> <b>Resolution:</b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Move away from the mortal, leaving the scene.</span><br /> <b>Beat: </b><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Attempt to talk down, or attack the mortal.</span></span></span></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Holy Ground</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Mortal places of faith, imbued with the divine shard from above, is anathema to demons. The Heavenly Host has spent millenia turning the human mind, and self against all that the demons are, and stand for. While in a place of great faith, the psychic residue and disdain for the Fallen concentrates. While on this ground the Fallen suffers a penalty to all actions that ranges from -1 to -5, as the holy rage and pain fills his mind.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Consecrated Objects</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Just as a mortal's wrathful faith and abjuration can harm the Fallen, and just as holy places can burn the Fallen, so too does the blessed weapons of mortals greviously injure the demon. When an object has been ritually prepared and imbued with the true belief of the mortals that it is holy, it does Bashing damage equal to the Fallen's permanent Torment rating. For example, a blessed sword , when used to strike a Fallen with 4 Torment, would do 4 extra Bashing damage on top of the damage it would normally do. The damage comes in the form of cracking, and burning flesh. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T17:08:26-07:00","id":220590,"title":"","content":"Maybe i've just misread or misinterpreted what you've said. But it seems like you're not merging DtF and DtD. But rather just giving DtF a rules update. Because you're pretty much stripping out everything that makes DtD it's own thing. You're even stripping the Machine out of the God-Machine leaving it as just ye olde generic demiurge.<br /> So how about this.<br /> Leave the God-Machine and it's ilk how they are, but also have the Fallen as remnants of the True Divinity that the GM overthrew to gain it's hold on reality. That way you can play up how 'different' and 'wrong' the GMs works are compared to how things should be for the Fallen, but you can also play up how 'ancient' and 'unknown' the Fallen are to the Unchained. Also by keeping both the Fallen and the Unchained in setting you can set them up as strange mirrors of each other, possibly to try to illustrate that the God-Machine stole knowledge and power, and that there are multiple things that can claim the title of 'Demon'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1696-redspine","name":"RedSpine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T19:01:13-07:00","id":220633,"title":"","content":"You've probably misinterpreted what my meaning was. The whole point of the exercise is to take everything I like about the Descent (the cold war between angels and demons, mainly) and the things I liked about Fallen, while chucking everything I did not like. The mixing them together into a coherent setting. As you can see, I really liked the flavor of the Fallen compared to the Unchained. I did not, however, like the emphasis on Faith and belief. I did not think it fit NWoD too well. Aether provided a thematic name for the stuff of the Divine.<br /> <br /> However, I like your idea. It has a certain ring to it. As it is right now, I'm still on mechanics for the Fallen. I'm gleefully pilfering the Unchained, and the old WoD rules. I have just a translation of DtF for NWoD, that's not what this is, but this is the compilation of everything my wife and I like from both (And Demon the Redemption) thrown together. I'd keep some of what I've written, which would change the Unchained, seeing as how Aether is the true energy of the divine, and not waste heat from Essence. What I'm saying is the setting assumptions I want to go with, will change the setting. On the other hand, my wife likes the idea of the God-Machine usurping the place of the True Divine. Now, I ask what would happen to the original Elohim? Did they become angels under the God-Machine?<br /> <br /> As an idea for that question, perhaps a council of Archangels built the God-Machine to compute, and take the place of the True Divine after it left the world. It was built using all the principles of 100 species, and all the Angels knew. When it was completed, they set it to run the universe, but isn't perfect. I'm not completely sold on the idea, but it's a fun tangent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 08-06-2014, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T01:06:52-07:00","id":221768,"title":"","content":"For today, we have Torment and the first Dominion I've done. My wife and I translated 5 or so Dominions form Demon: the Redemption fully, and translated the capabilities of others... we found them... kind of boring. (sorry Uxas! &gt;.&lt;) Okay, not all of them, but some of them we felt could use more flavor. So, we hashed out a system that was inspired by, but not, the original Dominion system.<br /> <br /> For those of you who don't know, the Dominion system of DtR was basically, you bought a power package. Only once, they were expensive (20 XP in the old system per) but they gave a lot of power. The powers were delineated by how much Faith you spent on the Evocation. To put another way, the 1 Faith cost power, and the 5 faith cost power were different abilities. (sometimes... other times it made the one power's numbers bigger)<br /> <br /> I'm going to take inspiration from that.<br /> <br /> Each Domain has 4 powers a Minor Evocation, a Lesser Evocation, a Median Evocation, and a Greater Evocation. They cost 0, 1, 2, 4 Aether in that order to use them. They cost 6 XP per Dominion and you start with two.<br /> <br /> But before we get to the Dominion of the Celestial, I want to present the rules on Torment.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Torment</span></b><br /> The Fallen have been locked up by the decree of the Elohim. They transgressed Heaven's law, and were punished accordingly. They committed sins too great to be unwritten from existence, or to be recycled into angels, untainted by the feelings they had, and the rebellious nature within. No. The Fallen were made an example of, locked in a place so far away from the Light of Creation, trapped in a place where reality is ragged, and unwhole, where they truly learned to hunger for the Aether they had supped from mortals in the previous War. It was a pain greater than fire, or needles, or even the pain of oblivion. It was a constant feeling of hunger, of distance from what made an angel what it was. It was a place of corruption, and sin... and Torment.<br /> Torment is a malefic force that resides locked in the psyche of all the Fallen. It's the collective corruption of the sins forgotten, and of an eternity spent in exile out of reality. But the prison was not perfect, when the Fallen flee the Depths, they are torn ragged, and weakened (humbled some might say) before they merge with the human host. The memories, the feelings and the <i>humanity</i> of their hosts changes the fallen angels in a fundamental way. They know more than rage, hunger and hate. With memories locked inside their shattered soul, the new Fallen is free from the burden.... but only for a short while.<br /> The corruption lurks beneath the skin, painful memories, and atrocities lie just beneath the surface of the Fallen's thoughts, many of them without context, but they all come with feelings of anguish, and wrath. With these feelings comes the dark energy known as Torment. It seeks only to feast, destroy and defile. It is the birthright of the Fallen, a sin they made for themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Torment Rolls</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Resolve + Composure<br /> <b>Dice Pool Modifiers</b><br /> <i>Torment 9 \u2013 10</i>: -2<br /> <i>Torment 6 \u2013 8</i>: -1<br /> <i>Torment 3 \u2013 5:</i> +0<br /> <i>Torment 2 \u2013 1:</i> +2<br /> <i>Point of Aether above turn limit:</i> -1<br /> (Example, if you use a Greater Evocation when you can only spend 1 Aether per turn, you get a -3 to your Torment roll)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Intentionally Invoking Torment</b><br /> Intentionally evoking Torment is a risky move. It's filling the Fallen's heart with hate, and pain, and anger. There is no point to do so unless the Fallen wants to hurt the target, and hurt them badly. Gain 1 temporary Torment when the Fallen intentionally Evokes the Tormented aspect of his Evocation. Apply the normal Torment rules for by-standards harmed by this Evocation normally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dominion of the Celestial</span></b><br /> It is said from Aether all things spring, it is the divine essence, and that which sparks the soul of sentient beings, like humans. The core of the Fallen is made up of their Aether, it houses their memory, their forms and transmits them between all the realms of the universe. It was the first of the Elohim's task to distribute the Aether and start the process of the universe's formation. To this day, Dominion over the celestial essence of Aether is prized among the Fallen. The Dominion of the Celestial is about finding, manipulating and transmitting the essence of Heaven that is known as Aether.<br /> <b>System:</b> Learning the Dominion of the Celestial gives you the Minor Evocation of Lamp of Faith, the Lesser Evocation of Celestial Visions, the Median Evocation of Fires of Heaven, and the Greater Evocation of the Hand of God.<br /> <br /> <b>Minor Evocation: Lamp of Faith</b><br /> Using the Evocation the Demon can sense in the same range as their Aetheric Senses the reservoir of Aether a mortal has in it's soul. The Aether inside the mortal's soul appears like a luminous, white light that comes from within the mortal's core, a Fallen instinctively knows what the levels of light correspond too. Also, the Demon can see the crackling energy appear around other creatures who have an Aether pool as a radiant aura.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Occult + Reminiscence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 0 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Immediately roll Torment at a -2, gain the Spooked condition if you fail the Torment roll, as the appearance of sin and darkness manifests in a very grotesque fashion.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: The Evocation fails.<br /> <b>Success</b>: On a success, everyone in range's aura of Aether appears, and the player knows what Soul Strength of each mortal in range has, and how much Aether a each creature in the range has in their Aether pool.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Count your Reminiscence as two higher for purposes of range, and get the Inspired condition.<br /> <b>Torment:</b> On a failed Torment roll, count your Reminiscence as 4 higher than it is for range, but you see the black wounds of the soul instead of their radiance. You can tell what the Integrity (or similar stat) of all you can see, manifesting as bleeding wounds or dark wisps of energy. The Torment of your fellow Fallen is especially evident, and manifests before your eyes giving them a monstrous, wounded appearance.<br /> <br /> <b>Lesser Evocation: Celestial Visions</b><br /> The Fallen all can speak to one another by invoking the Names of their brethren. This is an aspect of Aether, an energy that comes from the Monad, the Unity, and binds life, matter and energy together. Using this principle, the Fallen can communicate despite any distance. This Evocation takes that same principle to the extreme; with it a Fallen can invoke any target within line of sight, or any target with a Celestial or True Name at any distance, and send them visions that are like a waking dream. Using this Evocation, the generals in the War in Heaven could give detailed, elaborate orders from any distance to any target. During the same war, it was also discovered that you can use it to Torment a foe from any range. When sending antagonistic visions penalize the roll by the target's Resolve + Reminiscence.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Expression + Reminiscence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Aether<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Immediately roll Torment again at a -2. You are also sent corresponding visions that have the same effect as if you rolled an Exceptional Success on yourself.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> You fail to convey any information through this power.<br /> <b>Success:</b> For each Success you can convey one piece of information (a sentence, a small scene or description), with antagonistic visions, it levies a situational -2 penalty to actions of concentration.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: With helpful messages, the target gains the Inspired Condition as a feeling of being watched and guided from above fills them. For antagonistic visions, the target gets<br /> <b>Torment:</b> The visions sent invariably turn dark, and torturous tinged by the malefic influence of Torment. Targets take the Demon's Torment in Bashing damage as their nose bleeds, and their brain is assaulted by horrific visions that wrack their brain.<br /> <br /> <b>Median Evocation: Fires of Heaven</b><br /> Aether is a fiery, and powerful substance that blazed forth into the material world. It is the basis for all energy and matter (so say the Fallen) but in it's natural state it is a divine flame, the same flame some say Prometheus stole for humankind. To the knowledgeable they can incite Aether's natural inclination to burn and stir it into a destructive force. The Fallen channels his Aether into his target. Pure white flame erupts from inside the target consuming them from the inside out. This fire is non-flammable, and will not catch anything it touches on fire.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Wits + Occult + Reminiscence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> Cost: 2 Aether<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The spent Aether burns out of you in fire, take 2 Lethal damage, and gain the Blinded tilt.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> This Evocation fails to go off.<br /> <b>Success</b>: For every success, Do 1 point of Lethal damage, and burn one point of the targets Aether, removing it from their pool.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>The blazing power of Evocation blinds the target. Target gets the Blinded tilt.<br /> <b>Torment: </b><br /> <br /> <b>Greater Evocation: Hand of God</b><br /> When an Evocation is used within your line of sight, you can activate this power to take control of the Evocation, turning a flame against it's owner, or using the healing energies of an Evocation to benefit an ally. If you roll more Success than the initiator\u2019s activation roll, you pick the target an intensity of the Evocation. If the initiator has more Aether per turn to spend, you can spend that on the Evocation.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Occult + Reminiscence<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4 Aether<br /> <br /> <b>Roll Result</b><br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Aether of the controlled Evocation goes violent, becoming unstable. You take 4B damage and are Blinded feedback of Aetheric currents.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> You fail to take control of the Evocation.<br /> <b>Success:</b> You take control of the initiator\u2019s Evocation, using it to your own benefit. You can redirect it's target to where you wish, and spend any extra Aether per turn that the target has left.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> You get the Inspired condition as the feeling of the Divine enters you. Or the rush of commanding.<br /> <br /> <b>Torment:</b> Your Torment effects the Evocation that you take control of, perverting and twisting it. Add your activation roll Success to the Evocation you take control of, and instantly make the Evocation uses it's Tormented version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T16:03:00-07:00","id":224574,"title":"","content":"All the First House's Dominions are done! Have a look here <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mA35coEuBRSJFHY-C5_2rZqaIkurEsC0jwZAs7VpYo8/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...ZAs7VpYo8/edit</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T00:34:17-07:00","id":225737,"title":"","content":"For symetry's sake, maybe the Namaru should only choose from Vocal or Cocophany Formula? Either they embraced their role as the bringers of the Lord's will (Vocal) or they reject his Creation (Cocophany).<br /> <br /> That said, I'm still trying to figure out how Dominions work...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T07:31:23-07:00","id":225941,"title":"","content":"That's funny, that what I originally had the Devils as, but I changed it for sake of ease.<br /> Dominion work buy you buy the Dominion for a large chunk of XP and you get the powers. You remember your Dominion, congratz! However, they are expensive, require Torment rolls, and if you spend more Aether per turn than you can naturally spend, it has a greater chance to be Tormented. They are powerful packages, mainly based off of the Dominion system from Redemption, but I've changed them a bit to be a bit more evocative.<br /> Edit: Also added the main doc to the first post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":1601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","user":"Dreaminggod","date":". 08-12-2014, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T20:21:45-07:00","id":227555,"title":"","content":"Alright, thinking on the mismatch of Houses and Embeds, I thought, &quot;Why not just add Incarnations to the game?&quot; So you'd have Incarnation (What your Duty was), House (What aspect of creation you were created to guide, control, create, ect) and Creed (what you do with your demonic existence) So you could have a Halaku Destroyer, which is pretty defining, or a Halaku Psychopomp that leads the dead to their place. Maybe an Halaku Messenger, who went to pronounce the death of important people, facts or ect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T02:25:53-07:00","id":232620,"title":"","content":"Well, latest rendition of the game, and I've made a lot of changes. Finding the Creation Edge's game (<a href=\"http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.com/demon-the-fallen-nwod\" target=\"_blank\">http://creationsedgegames.wikidot.co...he-fallen-nwod</a>) and my wife, and other player fell in love with the free-form Evocation. Now, I've updated them to the rules but, on reflection, I removed Embeds from the Fallen. I'm not sure if that's the best idea. My thought was any Embed (Should) be able to be mimiced by the Lores. However, I don't know if that's a smart idea, since Lores are all subject to Torment, and (ideally) the Embeds would not be. Any ideas? Thoughts?<br /> <br /> New Google Doc: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1W90AVFyoKn54bTtUPNsLDqDYmTSaGVWOiMMgYICqqfs/edit#heading=h.ka0ar91y0b40\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...h.ka0ar91y0b40</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","dat